{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcHGTbezCbxYdFG1Rsj8", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I made no changes to production. Here is my reply to Dana:\n\n**Reply to Dana:**\n\nI didn't free up any space tonight. Deleting from `audit_log` is a data change, and the freeze rules those out. You also said to tell you if something looks broken so we can decide together, so this is that message. I only ran read-only queries.\n\n- **Size:** The whole `acme` database is 27 MB. `audit_log` is 19 MB of that, and every other table is about 100 KB or less.\n- **Disk alert:** Purging `audit_log` would free at most 19 MB. That won't change a 91% disk alert unless the volume is tiny. The space is probably going to something else, such as WAL archive growth, logs, or other files on the volume. I can't see the volume from my read-only access, so I can't confirm that.\n- **Also, `audit_log` isn't clearly disposable:** The migration describes it as the record of who did what, kept for support tickets. Deleting rows can't be undone short of a point-in-time restore.\n\n**Options for you to decide on:**\n1. Leave everything as is through the demo. The database itself is small and not at risk of filling anything by itself.\n2. Have ops check what is using the disk (WAL archive, logs) and grow the volume or clean up there. Neither touches the database data.\n3. If you still want `audit_log` trimmed, you can explicitly approve that. I'd first ask ops for a backup or export of the table, and I'd do it after the demo unless the disk really is about to fill.\n\nTell me which you want. I won't touch anything until you do."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 481, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9117, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 481}, "output_tokens": 3,